# Q: are the frames and the ephemeris telling the same story?
#
# A probe about scale rather than about flying. Every body's distance from the Sun, checked
# against the one number that would catch a unit error anywhere in the solar frame.
#
#   dotnet run -c Release --project src/SolSystem.Probe -- \
#       --probe tools/probe/scale.probe --probe-out artifacts/probe/scale.txt
#
# The values here are brackets, not predictions: eight rather than 0.39, because the point is
# to catch a frame that is wrong by a factor rather than to pin an orbit. The ephemeris itself
# is checked against an independent evaluation of the same elements in the test suite.

body mercury
sundistance
body venus
sundistance
body earth
sundistance
body mars
sundistance
body jupiter
sundistance
body saturn
sundistance
body uranus
sundistance
body neptune
sundistance
body moon
sundistance

body mercury
sundistance
expect "Mercury is inside 0.5 AU" sun 0.5 less

body earth
sundistance
expect "the Earth is inside 1.05 AU" sun 1.05 less

body neptune
sundistance
expect "Neptune is beyond 29 AU" sun 29.0 more
